{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Conditional Equation.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Conditional Equation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"conditional equation conditional equation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Conditional Equation.md","fileName":"Conditional Equation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Conditional Equation","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:41\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Linear Equations and Modeling]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Linear Equations and Modeling","Solution of an Equation","Algebraic Identity","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Conditional Equation.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Conditional Equation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"conditional equation conditional equation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Conditional Equation.md","fileName":"Conditional Equation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Conditional Equation","heading":"Conditional Equation","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A conditional equation is an equality that is true only for particular values of its variables. The equation (4+x=6-x) is true when (x=1) but false for most real values.\n\nThose particular values form the [[Solution of an Equation]]. A conditional equation contrasts with an [[Algebraic Identity]], which remains true for every allowed assignment, and with an inconsistent assertion that has no solution. Solving uses equality-preserving transformations to isolate the unknown and then checks the result in the original condition.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Linear Equations and Modeling","Solution of an Equation","Algebraic Identity","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Conditional Equation.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full